face-image: img/All_Quiet.jpg

= All Quiet on the Western Front

The Allied film *All Quiet on the Western Front*, based on the Commonwealth novel *Im Westen nichts Neues* by Erich Maria Remarque, is a film about the experiences of Commonwealth soldiers in the Great War, and how they gradually became disillusioned with the ideas of patriotism and nationalism. 

As an anti-war film, it is the target of major protest by <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> actors, especially the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> and the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span>. They are calling for the government to ban the film. If we do not ban it, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> threatens to violently stop the film from being shown or watched.

- @ban: Ban the film, to prevent <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> violence.
- @allow: Allow the film to be shown.
- @allow_protect: Allow the film to be shown, and use the Heartland police to prevent <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> disruptions.
- @everyone: In fact, everyone needs to learn the lessons of this film. Give free tickets to students and government employees.

@ban
on-arrival: guild_royalist += 5; burgher_royalist += 3; commons_royalist += 2; disfavored_royalist += 2; loyalist_strength += 50; nationalism += 6; pro_republic -= 5

When we ban the film, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> immediately celebrate it as a major victory; they claim that even the red Vaelists agree with them! It is a major boost to their morale.


@allow
on-arrival: nationalism += 3; guild_royalist += 5; burgher_royalist += 3; commons_royalist += 1; disfavored_royalist += 1; loyalist_strength += 15; pro_republic -= 3; strife += 1

While we allow the film, showings are marred by violence. Showings of the film eventually stop, and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> claim victory.


@allow_protect
choose-if: heartland_police_loyalty >= 0.65 and ((heartland_leader = "Bristol" or heartland_leader = "Pendrigon") or unionist_relation >= 65)
unavailable-subtitle: [? if heartland_police_loyalty < 0.65:The police are not willing to protect the film. ?] [? if not heartland_leader = "Bristol" and not heartland_leader = "Pendrigon" and unionist_relation < 65: Our coalition partners restrain us from policing actions. ?]
on-arrival: nationalism -= 4; pro_republic += 4*(1-dissent); strife += 1

Under the protection of the police, the people are allowed to watch the film in peace. <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> disturbances are kept to a minimum.

@everyone
choose-if: heartland_police_loyalty >= 0.75 and heartland_leader = "Bristol" or heartland_leader = "Pendrigon"
unavailable-subtitle: [? if heartland_police_loyalty < 0.75: The police are unable to guarantee the safety of all the attendees. ?] [? if not heartland_leader = "Bristol" and not heartland_leader = "Pendrigon": Our coalition partners restrain us from this action. ?]
on-arrival: nationalism -= 5; pro_republic += 5*(1-dissent); commons_royalist -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; burgher_royalist -= 3

Under police protection, crowds throng the film's showings, as <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> protest outside. The reception is mixed, but a new national conversation develops, reexamining the right-wing histories of the war. Quietly, many minds are changed, or at least affected in subtle ways.

